<div class="abstract">
  <div class="label">Abstract</div>
  <p>
    Which content pages should an editor review for a refresh first, given limited time?
    Using FlyRank's anonymized content-performance data and a production-scale search
    data warehouse (~79M rows, queried directly with DuckDB), I built a Random Forest
    ranking model and compared it against a transparent, hand-written baseline rule on
    an identical client-holdout test split. The learned model reached a measured
    Precision@50 of <b>0.540</b>, versus <b>0.240</b> for the baseline rule, on the same
    split and metric. A full leakage audit — including a deliberate leak test — confirmed
    the result reflects real signal rather than memorized client patterns. The output is
    packaged as a ranked, reason-coded action playbook intended strictly as decision
    support for a human editor, not as an autonomous publishing system.
  </p>
</div>

